{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731254Z","id":"aa1344c28799fc184a41e2f18b50fc3751794d662961edb93a0ce5c4df9f3d0b","body":{"detail":"While a page's own scripts hold up the parse, comment mode and use() wait for it with no sign to the viewer. This needs a protocol addition: the bridge reports that it is waiting.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":26},"end":{"line":29},"content_hash":"21752b7263ca6b42a47eaef764ade6ba85f1d6e668c14f22c1a65849231a7eb0"},"suggested_fix":"Have the bridge report a wait for the parse, and the shell show a hint ('waiting for the page').","summary":"The shell shows nothing while the bridge waits for the page's parse","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:16:01.905107Z","id":"e345bb553d4e3e680daad70f7c5d05ec91d0b38821fb38154b5e3ce95f874fef","body":{"detail":"While a page's own scripts hold up the parse, comment mode and use() wait for it with no sign to the viewer. This needs a protocol addition: the bridge reports that it is waiting.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":29},"end":{"line":32},"content_hash":"21752b7263ca6b42a47eaef764ade6ba85f1d6e668c14f22c1a65849231a7eb0"},"suggested_fix":"Have the bridge report a wait for the parse, and the shell show a hint ('waiting for the page').","summary":"The shell shows nothing while the bridge waits for the page's parse","supersedes":"aa1344c28799fc184a41e2f18b50fc3751794d662961edb93a0ce5c4df9f3d0b","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.151745Z","id":"3f266ae83272f0220b862e118174c5b0b9fdeaf0aa0c63d555a38f5e193522f9","body":{"detail":"While a page's own scripts hold up the parse, comment mode and use() wait for it with no sign to the viewer. This needs a protocol addition: the bridge reports that it is waiting.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":31},"end":{"line":34},"content_hash":"21752b7263ca6b42a47eaef764ade6ba85f1d6e668c14f22c1a65849231a7eb0"},"suggested_fix":"Have the bridge report a wait for the parse, and the shell show a hint ('waiting for the page').","summary":"The shell shows nothing while the bridge waits for the page's parse","supersedes":"e345bb553d4e3e680daad70f7c5d05ec91d0b38821fb38154b5e3ce95f874fef","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/long-press.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:56:14.752276Z","id":"a4e0fc3d2449cef6e4c9e5c62dbf3e8fb48354924f9738b81f8f488f38ead924","body":{"detail":"The tests in web/bridge/test/long-press.test.ts and comment-mode.test.ts dispatch synthetic TouchEvents in jsdom. Three browser behaviours they cannot show: (1) that the cancelled touchend still grants the frame user activation, which the shell requires before it takes clax:pick-start (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md section 3.5); (2) that Android Chrome/WebView still delivers touchend, not touchcancel, after the long-press contextmenu that comment-mode.ts cancels; (3) that no click is synthesized after the cancelled touchend (comment-mode.ts swallows one within 800 ms in case it is).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":117},"end":{"line":127},"content_hash":"571b41cf4f06dcc085a48acdbdbb6ab4e2f8e92aa64da6e4cecd98a8a433efd1"},"suggested_fix":"Exercise a long-press in the Playwright app-mode e2e with touch emulation (hasTouch) and on an Android device or emulator, and confirm a composer opens with a clip.","summary":"Long-press pick on a real Android WebView is unverified: activation, contextmenu and touchcancel","tags":["needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/scroll.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:56:14.752447Z","id":"e941822a7ca1c95d030d297f6a807ef7f3fddb5f5be19dda259c85474a638073","body":{"detail":"While the document is too short to reach y, restoreScroll retries every 100 ms for up to 2000 ms and then scrolls to y. If the viewer scrolls the new version during that wait, the restore still moves the page under them once the document grows.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":44},"end":{"line":56},"content_hash":"976d3a24272d77f4d4c99c457071ba7ccbbcea345f4836021a184237edf283ff"},"suggested_fix":"Stop the retries on a trusted wheel, touchmove or keydown in the page before the restore lands.","summary":"restoreScroll does not yield to the viewer's own scroll while it waits","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:56:14.752506Z","id":"aabe69cd6f81820782d1b558cd5fc3b9df0de3213206994250b602d2c24795ee","body":{"detail":"Measured with esbuild (minified, gzip -9) from the bridge source before and after commit 647958f22844: eager bridge 5056 -> 5413 bytes, comment part 10766 -> 11644 bytes. Budgets are bridge 5501 and partComment 11821, recorded as measured size plus 10 percent, so both still fit, with under 200 bytes of headroom each. Not measured with scripts/bundle-size.mjs against a full npm run build.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":59},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"015be019c0dd9e8ca33aafae42fbc53ff955e37b8a61197bc513fdb116f567da"},"summary":"The scroll report grows the eager bridge by about 360 bytes gzip, close to web/perf/bundle-budget.json","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:01:58.540247Z","id":"f5d81f85a7f4e426405c8bb680f190b7a2517d18140e69087da45b0f50e5f592","body":{"detail":"Failure: in comment mode with a mouse, a plain drag over text (no Shift, no Option) no longer selects text, so onUp finds a collapsed selection and the click that follows picks the enclosing element instead of a range. Option+drag selection widening likewise picks the wrong element. set(true) cancels selectstart (line 125) and setGuard adds GUARD_CSS (line 54: user-select:none on html) for every input type, not only touch. Reproduced: `CLAX_TEST_BIN=<debug clax> npx playwright test e2e/area.spec.ts -g 'plain text drag|drag selection made with Option'` fails 4/4 at commit 647958f22844 ('Expected: range, Received: element' at area.spec.ts:179; '#panel' for '#para' at area.spec.ts:294). A bare Chromium page with the same style and selectstart listener confirms a mouse drag selects nothing. The jsdom tests in web/bridge/test/comment-mode.test.ts set selections programmatically and cannot see it. Right-click menus in comment mode are also cancelled on desktop now.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":120},"end":{"line":131},"content_hash":"159eeceaa541441fdc5b42a209f0f871671e4558de278914c95bc589a426ee79"},"suggested_fix":"Scope the guard to touch: cancel selectstart and contextmenu only while a LongPress hold is in progress (between touchstart and its end or abandon), or add the user-select style only for that span, and keep -webkit-touch-callout:none (which has no mouse effect). Re-run e2e/area.spec.ts.","summary":"The selection guard breaks mouse drag-select comments on desktop and in the extension overlay","tags":["review","task:W1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:01:58.540469Z","id":"4858358cf08573e04b7597aff73fccdba719df2e55b82edce3bdf40e69ea1a3a","body":{"detail":"Failure: in the browser shell with touch (Playwright hasTouch/isMobile, 390x800, subdomain and sandbox), entering comment mode by the Comment button (tap or click), then a CDP Input.dispatchTouchEvent touchStart held 800 ms on an <h2> and touchEnd: the bridge outlines the target (one clax:hover) and posts clax:pick-start, navigator.userActivation.isActive is true in the shell, but document.activeElement in the shell is still the Comment BUTTON, so frameGesture() (web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts, rule 2: focus in the content frame) refuses the start and no composer opens. A short tap on the same point opens the composer (control passes). The cancelled touchend suppresses the compatibility mousedown that would focus the frame, and touchPick does not call focusPage() as the area drag's press does (line 406). Activation itself is granted on the cancelled touchend.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":374},"end":{"line":381},"content_hash":"75cbd53400d882431e5fe2bf404faa3bbb216cd9245c54a96684b19db6182397"},"suggested_fix":"Call focusPage() in touchPick (or on arm) before pickAt, then confirm gesture.ts rule 3 counts the arrival for a touch hold (a mouseover may not be sent for a long-press); pin it with the long-press e2e in web/e2e/app-mode.spec.ts, asserting the composer opens.","summary":"A long-press pick is refused by the shell: focus never enters the frame","tags":["review","task:W1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:01:58.540556Z","id":"b4d28b681aba3256637167ca47d3819e901091b3510a4f945d89acdfbcffb662","body":{"detail":"Measured with web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs on full `npm run build`s of git archives of 647958f22844^ and 647958f22844: eager bridge 5462 -> 5821 (+359; budget 5501), artifact entry 64006 -> 64008 (+2; budget 64006), comment part 10825 -> 11714 (+889; budget 11821, 107 left), extension overlay 17979 -> 18922. So scripts/quality_gates.sh's bundle lane fails until web/perf/bundle-budget.json is raised. The eager growth is reportScroll and the restore handler, which only the app shell (welcome app: true) uses.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":274},"end":{"line":274},"content_hash":"c369ab4b89d3932cfe40469d0c393fbb0ade276010f99c29b465d48bfe20a834"},"suggested_fix":"Load scroll.ts as a lazy bridge part on the app welcome so browsers outside the app pay nothing, or raise the bridge and artifact budgets by the measured growth in the same branch before the gates run.","summary":"bundle-size.mjs fails at 647958f22844: eager bridge 5821 > 5501 and artifact 64008 > 64006","tags":["review","task:W1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:01:58.540605Z","id":"99ab96e8c2f6a3fdd6757b08b5dff94b5485c79044c811ab6ad116be3bad23ef","body":{"detail":"LongPress.onEnd cancels the touchend (web/bridge/src/long-press.ts:125), so Chromium synthesizes no click after a long-press pick; the swallow window set in touchPick (line 379) then consumes the next genuine click within 800 ms instead, for example a quick tap after a refused pick. Nothing tests that no click arrives.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":450},"end":{"line":455},"content_hash":"eaaddc1804a6d9296a16c6f4e183253b6d32303658c0017de1c7c36df32bd72d"},"suggested_fix":"Swallow only a click whose coordinates match the pick's release point within the slop, or drop the window if the e2e shows no click follows a cancelled touchend.","summary":"The 800 ms click swallow eats the viewer's next real tap or click","tags":["review","task:W1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/scroll.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:01:58.540646Z","id":"a9fc8068284b1850905aa45b8b0431893d3961612ca271450e73fa3d6c6d52e7","body":{"detail":"When the newer version is shorter than y, restoreScroll retries for 2000 ms and gives up without scrolling, so the viewer lands at the top rather than as close to their place as the page allows.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":44},"end":{"line":56},"content_hash":"976d3a24272d77f4d4c99c457071ba7ccbbcea345f4836021a184237edf283ff"},"suggested_fix":"At the deadline, scroll to min(y, scrollHeight - innerHeight).","summary":"A restore past the new version's end leaves the page at the top","tags":["review","task:W1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:01:58.540698Z","id":"d62518b324b51f6b00e30488bc5fdf2e8c2b4b6e9adf3257e0f45eaa56093680","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"aabe69cd6f81820782d1b558cd5fc3b9df0de3213206994250b602d2c24795ee","span":{"start":{"line":59},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"015be019c0dd9e8ca33aafae42fbc53ff955e37b8a61197bc513fdb116f567da"},"summary":"Measured with scripts/bundle-size.mjs on full builds: both bridge and artifact are over budget, not under (eager bridge 5462 -> 5821 vs 5501; artifact 64006 -> 64008 vs 64006). See the concern on web/bridge/src/bridge.ts:274.","tags":["review","task:W1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:56.332445Z","id":"8bda8cc49a801038553a0b0305a28b216a661c046600d1dfe1d5c87b7792bebb","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed in 647958f22844: selectstart and contextmenu are cancelled only while LongPress.holding (a finger down), and the guard style is only -webkit-touch-callout:none. Evidence: `CLAX_TEST_BIN=<stable debug clax> npx playwright test e2e/area.spec.ts -g 'plain text drag|drag selection made with Option'` after a fresh npm run build: 4 passed. Regression test web/bridge/test/comment-mode.test.ts 'mouse_selection_and_context_menu_are_untouched' passes (fails against 647958f22844).","supersedes":"f5d81f85a7f4e426405c8bb680f190b7a2517d18140e69087da45b0f50e5f592","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:56.332640Z","id":"c22819e7cf0ea470c4879168127b510321fd62127f659b6aee122c3cf5159769","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed in 647958f22844: the long-press no longer cancels touchend. In Chromium the release is then followed by the browser's compatibility mouse events and click, which deliver a trusted mouseover of iframe.frame to the shell (the counted arrival) and move focus into the frame; the click picks through onClick. With touchend cancelled the shell saw no pointer event at all during or after the hold (diagnosed with a capture listener on the shell window). When no click follows within TOUCH_CLICK_WAIT_MS, comment mode calls focusPage() and picks itself. Evidence: `npx playwright test e2e/long-press.spec.ts` (hasTouch, isMobile, 390x800, CDP touchStart held 800 ms then touchEnd, subdomain and sandbox): 4 passed, composer visible with its textarea focused; the same spec failed 4 of 4 at 647958f22844 (focusPage on a cancelled release). Wider run of area, bridge-comment, comment-targets, comment-flows, bridge-parts and long-press specs: 76 passed.","supersedes":"4858358cf08573e04b7597aff73fccdba719df2e55b82edce3bdf40e69ea1a3a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:56.332772Z","id":"7c515fdb25b89fccc4d94fa9e254c96cc25035896c2944785878f1784c481649","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed in 647958f22844 (the 800 ms swallow went in 647958f22844): no click is swallowed. The browser's click after a long-press release is the pick itself, and it clears the TOUCH_CLICK_WAIT_MS fallback timer. Evidence: web/bridge/test/comment-mode.test.ts 'the browser's click after a long-press picks, once' and 'leaves the viewer's next click after a long-press pick to pick again' pass.","supersedes":"99ab96e8c2f6a3fdd6757b08b5dff94b5485c79044c811ab6ad116be3bad23ef","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:56.332895Z","id":"c9b4cd808bfbb762f0e0d3bd83574724c6cda0d88ab2becd3ad5928040101176","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed in 647958f22844: scroll.ts moved into the caps part, loaded on a welcome with app: true; the restore position rides on that welcome (restoreScroll), removing the clax:restore-scroll handler from the eager bridge; clax:scroll left out of BRIDGE_TYPES until the shell takes it. Evidence: npm run build plus node scripts/bundle-size.mjs on a copy of web/ at 647958f22844: 'gzip bytes: gallery 27771, artifact 64006, questions 14192, eager bridge 5492, parts: comment 11722, clip 15004, caps 8492, ...' with no budget exceeded (bridge 5501, artifact 64006, partComment 11821, partCaps 8773).","supersedes":"b4d28b681aba3256637167ca47d3819e901091b3510a4f945d89acdfbcffb662","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/scroll.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:56.333012Z","id":"4144835cf19ac306a93502ac47772d7cdcca6d1b6519674bdbedd8fa0448f665","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed in 647958f22844: at the 2000 ms deadline restoreScroll scrolls to min(y, scrollHeight - innerHeight), never below 0. Evidence: web/bridge/test/scroll.test.ts 'after 2000 ms in all, scrolls as far towards the position as the document reaches' and 'after 2000 ms, a document shorter than the viewport stays at the top' pass (both failed before the change).","supersedes":"a9fc8068284b1850905aa45b8b0431893d3961612ca271450e73fa3d6c6d52e7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:56.333127Z","id":"841f9526f64e2390e80ffeab58ddd7133ae973ece3f1525b83ccc4e019e5ff53","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"The esbuild estimate here was wrong (see reply d62518b3: the gate measured 5821). Superseded by the fix for b4d28b68 in 647958f22844: the eager bridge measures 5492 against 5501.","supersedes":"aabe69cd6f81820782d1b558cd5fc3b9df0de3213206994250b602d2c24795ee","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/long-press.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:56.333273Z","id":"8cc89df609baf79c6898d7d444ed713bf4c7a923c04b9d99a7417398c63ef2f2","body":{"detail":"web/e2e/long-press.spec.ts proves the pick in desktop Chromium with touch emulation, where a CDP hold of 800 ms released without a cancelled touchend is followed by mousemove, mousedown, mouseup and click (no contextmenu): the click picks, and its mouseover of iframe.frame and focus entry satisfy frameGesture() in web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts. On Android a real long-press raises GestureLongPress and contextmenu (cancelled while LongPress.holding) and may send no click after the release. Then comment-mode.ts touchPick picks after TOUCH_CLICK_WAIT_MS (400 ms) with focusPage(), and the shell takes it only if it counted the finger's arrival on the frame (rule 3), which nothing in the hold may provide: the pick would be refused. Also unverified: that touchend, not touchcancel, follows the cancelled contextmenu. The 400 ms wait is a guess at how late a click can come under load; a click later than that is blocked by the pick it raced (capturing).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":126},"end":{"line":134},"content_hash":"ae8608224a3fa6b35096501bd138682364ec9108ef497a680eb10d1fd2ac2115"},"suggested_fix":"Run the long-press on an Android device or emulator in the app (F8/F10). If the fallback pick is refused, the shell needs a touch arrival signal (for example a bridge-reported hold confirmed by the frame's activation), which is a change to gesture.ts's rules for the owner to decide.","summary":"Long-press on a real Android WebView is unverified: whether a click follows the release, and the no-click fallback's gesture","supersedes":"a4e0fc3d2449cef6e4c9e5c62dbf3e8fb48354924f9738b81f8f488f38ead924","tags":["needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/protocol.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:56.333418Z","id":"d86448df32848684cf8d6ac6b9fc30e6d076dabd8a0d5b9981b255c10ca2c05e","body":{"detail":"The bridge posts clax:scroll after a welcome with app: true (web/bridge/src/scroll.ts), but BRIDGE_TYPES omits it, so web/shell/src/bridge-link.ts drops it. It was left out because the string alone moves the artifact bundle from 64006 to 64008 gzip bytes, over web/perf/bundle-budget.json's artifact budget of 64006, and no shell code reads the message yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":137},"end":{"line":137},"content_hash":"493ddf5c20216e677c89e3b913b63684f8c244e029795a0042014575bdf9841c"},"suggested_fix":"When the app shell (plan Task W2) reads clax:scroll, add it to BRIDGE_TYPES in the same change, with the artifact budget raised for the shell's app mode.","summary":"clax:scroll is not in BRIDGE_TYPES: the shell drops the scroll report until its app mode adds it","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/protocol.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:20:28.379485Z","id":"2711ab9e277c70338403afa775453dd176bffd3671441c461bc856429ba47ff8","body":{"detail":"The shell answers each clax:hello with a welcome (web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts:1107), and the bridge re-sends hello on clax:greet (web/bridge/src/bridge.ts:279). appScroll (web/bridge/src/scroll.ts) restores every position a welcome carries (web/bridge/test/scroll.test.ts 'restores each position it is given'), so if the app shell keeps restoreScroll on later welcomes for the same document, the page jumps back under a viewer who has scrolled since.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"a570438535dc062bc2028c3ed5f90eaad066d3aa351ed711f39efcc8bfc3ef40"},"suggested_fix":"In the shell's app mode, put restoreScroll only on the first welcome after loading a newer version, and pin that with a controller test; or have the bridge honour it once per document.","summary":"Every welcome carrying restoreScroll scrolls again, including a re-greet's","tags":["review","task:W1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/protocol.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:41.152743Z","id":"360cfeebcd9d924aa2a8a994c1bba1b1128bf3ca486d57428cdea4d8bb20a005","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts ctl.app.welcome consumes the pending restore on the first welcome; test web/shell/src/app/host.test.ts 'auto_follow_loads_a_newer_version_and_asks_the_bridge_to_restore_scroll' checks a re-greet's welcome has no restoreScroll.","kind":"comment","references":"2711ab9e277c70338403afa775453dd176bffd3671441c461bc856429ba47ff8","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"a570438535dc062bc2028c3ed5f90eaad066d3aa351ed711f39efcc8bfc3ef40"},"summary":"Done in 647958f22844: the app shell puts restoreScroll only on the first welcome after a newer version loads","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/protocol.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:41.152786Z","id":"dfac0046c98d640dbaad35942761c4469c6586d52ea7698ead15bb810afd54cf","body":{"detail":"Budget effect recorded on web/shell/src/artifact-main.ts:18.","kind":"comment","references":"d86448df32848684cf8d6ac6b9fc30e6d076dabd8a0d5b9981b255c10ca2c05e","span":{"start":{"line":137},"end":{"line":137},"content_hash":"17d581a29ca62aed0ab5f96cfbdfa748a66a60e2360f4b050e862a6b1ee2ebfd"},"summary":"Done in 647958f22844: clax:scroll is in BRIDGE_TYPES and read by web/shell/src/app/host.ts (onMessage)","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/long-press.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:41.152905Z","id":"593939809708afa0264abab7f30142a2d60a4dc1cada2f8e1251f5e301b9b37e","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts hostArrival, web/shell/src/app/host.ts attestPointer; security reasoning in the waiver on host.ts:221:230. Still open: the Flutter side (plan Task F8) must call it on every pointer down and up its Listener sees over the WebView, in WebView CSS pixels, and a real Android run must confirm the pick is taken.","kind":"comment","references":"8cc89df609baf79c6898d7d444ed713bf4c7a923c04b9d99a7417398c63ef2f2","span":{"start":{"line":126},"end":{"line":134},"content_hash":"ae8608224a3fa6b35096501bd138682364ec9108ef497a680eb10d1fd2ac2115"},"summary":"Shell side of the no-click fallback built in 647958f22844: claxHost.attestPointer({x, y}) counts as the finger's arrival for 1 s in app mode","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/protocol.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:55.371626Z","id":"bf4ce4e84db9bf607bf5250bbc03f54bebadd8330f11804cfb57e7e6b7873152","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: web/shell/src/app/host.ts sends restoreScroll on the first welcome after auto-follow only; 'npx vitest run shell/src/app' 25 passed, incl. auto_follow_loads_a_newer_version_and_asks_the_bridge_to_restore_scroll (re-greet welcome has none)","supersedes":"2711ab9e277c70338403afa775453dd176bffd3671441c461bc856429ba47ff8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/protocol.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:55.475894Z","id":"7cb8bd3cac83beeef339c92afae8f4e37e02efbed14e0bb3e94b9b9d9140aa30","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: clax:scroll in BRIDGE_TYPES, read by web/shell/src/app/host.ts; e2e/app-mode.spec.ts 'a published version lands in place with the scroll kept' passed in both frame modes","supersedes":"d86448df32848684cf8d6ac6b9fc30e6d076dabd8a0d5b9981b255c10ca2c05e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/long-press.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:46:59.393843Z","id":"d7f96a3c8955415cea00c1bb8ccb1b51bb58b64d117172917819b272207bb98c","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart _attest and host_protocol.dart AttestPointer; covered by app_screen_test.dart 'every pointer down and up on the page is attested in page pixels'. A device run confirming the pick is taken is still needed (record on app_screen.dart:402:414).","kind":"comment","references":"8cc89df609baf79c6898d7d444ed713bf4c7a923c04b9d99a7417398c63ef2f2","summary":"Flutter side of the attestation built in f1c07f346b12: every pointer down and up over the WebView calls claxHost.attestPointer({pointer, phase, x, y}) in the page's CSS pixels","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:01:06.200394Z","id":"54f7434996060bfe6eac74c00fe13074660ab3034c0b6c12e1dd5ad25846e694","body":{"detail":"node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs at 647958f22844: 'bridge: 5508 gzip bytes, over its budget of 5501' (5493 at 647958f22844, measured from a clean archive of that commit). The growth is the desc key PickFlow.start posts and the part.desc(el) argument here; describe.ts itself is in the lazy comment part (11722 -> 11785, inside its 11821 budget). web/perf/bundle-budget.json is unchanged; Task W4 owns it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":176},"end":{"line":176},"content_hash":"731a435daaf3f9167f857c2cbe63f5ce5761f9f42b6d9bc212ece462aa9e5f29"},"suggested_fix":"Raise the bridge budget to 5565 (5501 + 15 rounded up to 64) in Task W4.","summary":"The eager bridge is 5508 gzip bytes, 7 over its 5501 budget, from the pick start's element description","tags":["budget","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:19:10.698336Z","id":"c08189738bafd4c7e2a66bad0b6c0560bab1ce76b765303830d82118085bd52a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Budget raised to 5565 in 647958f22844. node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs after a fresh scripts/build-web.sh: 'eager bridge 5508' with no budget exceeded, exit 0.","supersedes":"54f7434996060bfe6eac74c00fe13074660ab3034c0b6c12e1dd5ad25846e694","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/long-press.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:28:06.107592Z","id":"552b0eb0074586be23b5f3a8907ceabd3e76945f20f5791ac0939fb82b54f689","body":{"detail":"web/bridge/test/long-press.test.ts and comment-mode.test.ts ('hold, then drag') dispatch synthetic TouchEvents in jsdom, which always honour preventDefault. Three browser behaviours they cannot show: (1) that the touchmove crossing SLOP_PX after HOLD_MS is still cancelable on Android WebView and WKWebView, so the page does not scroll during the drag (Chrome ignores preventDefault on a touchmove it has already handed to scrolling, and sends touchcancel, which abandons the drag); (2) that the browser's long-press text selection (cancelled by comment-mode.ts onHeld on selectstart) does not instead grab the drag as a native selection handle drag; (3) that the selection made with Selection.setBaseAndExtent shows on a touch device with the ::selection tint set by CommentMode.setGuard (web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts:190).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":128},"end":{"line":144},"content_hash":"641474a8e7067be7f18a03348af3b7fe5da25f12fe15dbfa40a6d5c72ec4bd82"},"suggested_fix":"Exercise hold-drag in the Playwright e2e with touch emulation, and on an Android device and an iPhone/macOS WKWebView: hold 450 ms on text and drag, hold on an image and drag, and confirm no scroll, a tinted selection or a box, and a composer with the picked range or area.","summary":"Hold-then-drag on a real touch WebView is unverified: whether the move past the slop is still cancelable, and whether the browser's own long-press gesture takes the touch first","tags":["needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/long-press.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:28:06.107670Z","id":"f502853533814809ab544dc972d67fa2cca7c8a3e2fae89b42f50c48096c3871","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8cc89df609baf79c6898d7d444ed713bf4c7a923c04b9d99a7417398c63ef2f2","summary":"A hold-then-drag release (comment-mode.ts touchDragEnd) picks on touchend with no click to follow, as this record's no-click fallback does: it calls window.focus() first and relies on the same touchend activation and, in app mode, the host's pointer attestation (record 8cc89df6) for the shell to take the pick.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/inspect.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:39:06.892124Z","id":"18c8929cf710c68a7aa31eda0f300410ff654ff65b4753ed244be6b01e014e01","body":{"detail":"installErrorRing runs for every framed page (web/bridge/src/bridge.ts:103), not only the inspect view, which the bridge cannot know before its first script: devtools then attributes console.error calls to the bridge's wrapper, and the newest 20 calls' arguments stay referenced until they leave the ring (words are made only in errorsOf, in the clip part, to keep the eager bridge small). A page that replaces console.error without calling the function it replaced hides its later console errors from an inspection.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":52},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"04864742295da61691a5ba3a06124e59a08580af949fbcc95fc4d18572eb9812"},"summary":"The error ring wraps console.error on every framed page and keeps the logged values","tags":["inspect","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/inspect-render.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:39:06.892203Z","id":"d82ce354e2cbe7b1c54e512a57351ba028214d51ebc5775af4150f2aea93a0a1","body":{"detail":"web/bridge/test/bridge-inspect.test.ts mocks it; the crop (the body translated by its client box so the viewport sits in a w x h picture) and the opaque-origin sandbox path are unverified in a browser until the Playwright inspect spec (web/e2e/inspect.spec.ts) checks that ?inspect=1 returns a PNG of what the viewport shows.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":39},"content_hash":"09b9c9545b3a9c2ec3463fe9815eb9d8388bed37f56171e9aa83eb7805485959"},"summary":"renderViewport has run only as a stub under jsdom","tags":["inspect","test-gap","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:40:55.697663Z","id":"372b576877940ee25fc4479c97557dedc8140a569ed423939d8fb507d1d98a06","body":{"detail":"Failure: Chromium with hasTouch/isMobile (390x800), subdomain and sandbox modes, comment mode on via a tap on Comment; CDP Input.dispatchTouchEvent touchStart on #p (or on an <img>), held 800 ms, eight touchMoves 160 px right (or 120x100 down-right), touchEnd. The bridge builds the right anchor (range quote 'Grow revenue in ev', prefix/suffix set; area rect 120x100, area {x:0.3,y:0.25,w:0.4,h:0.5}), the page does not scroll and the selection is cleared, but clax:pick-start is answered clax:pick-refused and clax:pick arrives with clipError NOT_TAKEN. Cause: web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts checks frameGesture() synchronously on clax:pick-start, and its condition 3 (web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts header) needs the pointer's arrival on iframe.frame counted by a shell mouseover or a click; a touch that moved after a long-press sends no compatibility mouse events and no click, so the window.focus() in touchDragEnd moves focus but no arrival counts. A hold-release without a drag works only because Chromium sends mousemove/mousedown/mouseup/click after it (web/e2e/long-press.spec.ts). Unit tests in web/bridge/test/comment-mode.test.ts call hooks directly, so they cannot see the shell's refusal. Shell window had userActivation.isActive true and document.activeElement iframe.frame after the release.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":466},"end":{"line":498},"content_hash":"42eb9478a492d51288b76133396113f43f493a60525e1889904c307c7bd7c3ad"},"suggested_fix":"Needs a shell-side arrival for a touch drag outside app mode, or a confirming tap: e.g. keep the dragged selection or box after release and pick on the next tap inside it (its click brings the counted arrival), or have the bridge pick on the browser's click when one comes and otherwise show the hint. Then a Playwright spec (web/e2e/hold-drag.spec.ts, Task W7) asserting the composer opens with the range quote and the area rect in both frame modes.","summary":"In a browser on touch, a hold-then-drag pick is refused by the shell: the composer never opens and the pick carries 'it was not taken'","tags":["review","touch","gesture","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/long-press.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:40:55.697794Z","id":"732f781051fb5d7ce74ea33a54f80a56f415c7584443ef65425b28cde40a9c4c","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"552b0eb0074586be23b5f3a8907ceabd3e76945f20f5791ac0939fb82b54f689","summary":"Desktop Chromium touch emulation answers (1) and (2), not (3): after an 800 ms CDP hold, every touchmove was cancelable, preventDefault held the page at scrollY 0 through the drag, and no contextmenu, selectstart or touchcancel came; a 300 px swipe without the hold scrolled the page and posted no clax:pick-start. The ::selection tint was not checked, and a real Android WebView and WKWebView are still unverified. Separately, the pick these drags make is refused by the shell (blocker on web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts:466:498).","tags":["review","needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/inspect.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:50:26.736480Z","id":"402be07be21ecbc4c81fdfd7617a1f5939a32b89fa61aa6d5a5825508c9b16b4","body":{"detail":"The bridge grew from 5508 to 5915 gzip bytes (node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs on clean archives of f1c07f346b12 and 647958f22844), on every page's time-to-usable path. Only the capture has to run before the page's first script. installErrorRing also classifies each error event (element load failure vs script error), reads the failed URL and formats `at` eagerly (about 250 gzip bytes in dist/_clax/bridge.js), and the clax:inspect case in web/bridge/src/bridge.ts builds both posts and the error wording inline (about 115). Measured by substitution in the minified bridge: a ring that keeps raw [kind, event-or-args] pairs, with the split into errors/failed and the URL and position read in errorsOf, and a clax:inspect case that is one call into the clip part (which posts the answer itself), takes gzip -9 from 5956 to 5737 (-219).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":51},"end":{"line":72},"content_hash":"f9411b6dc3ad4438ca1adbe0166b8d5ba8abd7e84fe90f4914cc0ce1c15e46a4"},"suggested_fix":"Keep in installErrorRing only: one bounded list of [kind, ErrorEvent | PromiseRejectionEvent | console args], the console.error wrapper and the two listeners. Move element-vs-script classification, the URL read and the position to errorsOf (clip part); make the bridge's clax:inspect case call a clip-part function given (window, ring, message, post, clock, Observer).","summary":"About 220 of the eager bridge's 407 added gzip bytes need not be eager","tags":["perf","time-to-usable","review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/inspect-render.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:50:26.736539Z","id":"4871061ee5670c0e0e6909f2e3dacf1335259c8b6a72453fb36861c6a42d2fd6","body":{"detail":"Chromium, ?app=1&inspect=1, a page with <input placeholder=\"Your name\"> and <img src=\"missing-image.png\" alt=\"x\"> (404): the page shows the placeholder in the placeholder grey and the broken-image icon with its alt text; the inspection's PNG (renderViewport, modern-screenshot) shows \"Your name\" in the full text colour, as if typed, and a solid blue-violet box of about 25 x 20 px where the image is. The agent reads this PNG to judge its work, so it may take an empty field for a filled one and miss the broken image (failed lists the URL, so the latter is recoverable).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":39},"content_hash":"09b9c9545b3a9c2ec3463fe9815eb9d8388bed37f56171e9aa83eb7805485959"},"suggested_fix":"Paint ::placeholder text with the computed placeholder colour (or leave placeholders out) and draw a failed image as an outlined box with its alt text; or note in the tool result that placeholders and broken images are approximated.","summary":"The inspection PNG paints an input's placeholder as typed text and a broken image as a solid box","tags":["inspect","fidelity","review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/inspect-render.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:50:26.736587Z","id":"92fabf02f7fdfb3aa7837d5a3f6fac612d1382471c6e43a37ee2acf5daed0802","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"d82ce354e2cbe7b1c54e512a57351ba028214d51ebc5775af4150f2aea93a0a1","summary":"Run in Chromium with a temporary Playwright spec (not committed): subdomain and sandbox frames, with and without requestAnimationFrame, a hidden draft from POST /api/drafts, and a page scrolled to y=1500 all return a 390x800 PNG of what the viewport shows (the scrolled one shows the page's lower gradient); maxBytes 60% of the full PNG re-renders at 195x400 within the cap; maxBytes 50 answers 'the screenshot is over 50 bytes even at 0.125 scale'. The record stays open until a committed spec (web/e2e/inspect.spec.ts) covers it.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/inspect.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:50:26.736619Z","id":"c9eb05f7a214c00c63316b6fe83999191a567e640427fae0368d0fed8b6329b2","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"18c8929cf710c68a7aa31eda0f300410ff654ff65b4753ed244be6b01e014e01","summary":"The bridge can know the inspect view before its first script: the frame's browsing-context name (window.name, set by the shell as the iframe's name attribute before it loads) is readable synchronously by the frame's own first script. Installing the ring only when the shell names the frame for inspection would leave every browser-mode page's console.error attribution and retained arguments untouched, at no eager-byte cost.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T20:13:31.118281Z","id":"1e0e9471683d4f403b830f32224dd3a8563e19b16c657d3be53c410f97d78f7c","body":{"detail":"A touch that moved after a long-press brings no click and no compatibility mouse events, so the shell (web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts condition 3) never sees the finger arrive on the frame and refuses a pick made on touchend (record 372b5768). The release therefore keeps the selection, rectangle or outline with a chip beside it (CommentMode.showChip); the chip's tap is a real click in the frame, which gives the shell the arrival, and picks. A touch elsewhere, a scroll, a new drag or comment mode going off drops the offer, and the dropping touch's click picks nothing. In app mode (bridge.ts passes confirmDrag: () => !appShell) the host attests the finger and the release picks at once. The Chrome extension's overlay (web/extension/src/content/overlay-app.ts) passes no confirmDrag, so it shows the chip too, though no shell gesture rule applies there. Options not taken: pick on the browser's click when one comes and otherwise show a hint; count the frame's touch activation as an arrival in the shell (a page could then forge picks after any touch).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":527},"end":{"line":557},"content_hash":"708552a9e4c5ed2a5a5be4edb9af2dae3e020cce95ee6a67f533f6465fc3a1df"},"summary":"Decision (coordinator; the owner may overrule): in a browser, a hold-then-drag's release offers its pick with a 'Comment' chip instead of picking","tags":["decision","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T20:13:31.118480Z","id":"3e3a07f8ab5e0f27a82212b4d5eb100e3a05f7605f3407989b971f4d81c4a7ac","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: a browser hold-then-drag now offers its pick with a Comment chip whose tap (a real click) picks, and the shell takes it. Evidence: `npx playwright test e2e/hold-drag.spec.ts` -> 12 passed (twice), including subdomain and sandbox 'holding on text, then dragging along it, offers the range, and the chip's tap comments on it' and '... offers the area ...' asserting no clipError, a visible clip and a posted thread; `npx vitest run bridge shell` -> 1152 passed.","supersedes":"372b576877940ee25fc4479c97557dedc8140a569ed423939d8fb507d1d98a06","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/inspect.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:10:41.163764Z","id":"f30a871b36a9ebd0cdf271707cccd6a25e4fdefb17319ad6338b987c9f9d895e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"installErrorRing keeps only raw entries (events and console.error's arguments), errorsOf in the clip part classifies, reads URLs and positions, and the clax:inspect case is one call into the clip part (parts/clip.ts inspect). node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs on fresh builds: eager bridge 5934 gzip bytes on a clean archive of HEAD 647958f22844+W5 (647958f22844) vs 5754 with 647958f22844, -180; the remaining gap to the -219 estimate is the window.name gate of c9eb05f7 (INSPECT_FRAME constant and check) and the two-list split that keeps failed loads from pushing errors out (bridge/test/inspect.test.ts 'keeps RING_SIZE of each').","supersedes":"402be07be21ecbc4c81fdfd7617a1f5939a32b89fa61aa6d5a5825508c9b16b4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/inspect-render.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:10:41.165289Z","id":"3f1e2637b6a2336b76dca8da8260eb3ad948f3b4561e94065620230c4a899d22","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"faithfulClone (modern-screenshot onCloneEachNode) paints an empty field's clone in the field's ::placeholder colour and a failed image's clone as brokenImage (an outline, a picture icon and the alt text, at the image's size). Chromium, the built clip part's inspect() on a page with <input placeholder=\"Your name\"> and <img src=\"missing-image.png\" alt=\"Logo\"> (404): the PNG shows the placeholder grey as the page does and an outlined box with the icon and 'Logo'; bridge/test/inspect-render.test.ts 3/3 pass.","supersedes":"4871061ee5670c0e0e6909f2e3dacf1335259c8b6a72453fb36861c6a42d2fd6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/inspect.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:10:41.166602Z","id":"a339b59b7f82c1af62525f0c5b1c4b158c453918ae544e05661b61d56a95c0de","body":{"detail":"Since 647958f22844 the ring is installed only when the frame's window.name is INSPECT_FRAME (web/bridge/src/bridge.ts, web/shell/src/view/frame-host.ts names it in ?app=1&inspect=1), so other pages' console.error is the browser's (bridge/test/bridge-inspect-unnamed.test.ts). In the inspect frame the newest 20 calls' arguments and events stay referenced until they leave the ring, and a page that replaces console.error without calling the function it replaced hides its later console errors. A page may set its own window.name to clax-inspect: it then only keeps its own errors.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":52},"end":{"line":66},"content_hash":"51673e226b17daa00b02b5ec3a1cadb53e4b9cc8385de57a458bfaa352989936"},"summary":"In the inspect view's frame, the error ring wraps console.error and keeps the logged values","supersedes":"18c8929cf710c68a7aa31eda0f300410ff654ff65b4753ed244be6b01e014e01","tags":["inspect","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/inspect-render.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:08:27.683909Z","id":"5099ca0b15b3dac207c88b31247e6ad33fdf96de9d8039b273ae5528f1f32965","body":{"detail":"Measured in Chromium with a draft in the inspect view (web/e2e/inspect.spec.ts harness): on <style>body{margin:0}#r{position:absolute;left:30px;top:40px;...}</style><body><div id=r></div><p>hi</p>, the red box is at (30,72) in the PNG instead of (30,40); the <p>'s 16 px top margin collapses through the body in the page, so body.getBoundingClientRect().top is 16, but the clone (style margin 0, translated by box.top) does not collapse it, so content lands lower. With body{display:flow-root} the box is at (30,40). Separately, a page with an inline <img> that failed to load (40x40, beside a button) rendered everything below it 8 px lower than the page shows; with the image positioned absolutely the crop is exact (cause not isolated: faithfulClone's brokenImage glyph is a likely suspect). Pages with body{margin:0} and an h1 or p first are common, so the agent's render can be offset by one to two dozen pixels. inspect.spec.ts avoids both (h1 margin-top 0, the broken image absolute) to test the crop exactly.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":83},"end":{"line":83},"content_hash":"2c2c0cf7ab09a82c2509d809ec19816f847c6c7ebc1c221d7ccb3f54aa888402"},"suggested_fix":"Translate by the first rendered content's offset rather than the body's border box (for example give the clone root display:flow-root and translate by documentElement's client rect), and add an inspect.spec.ts case with a collapsing first-child margin and an inline broken image.","summary":"The inspection's screenshot is shifted down when a top margin collapses through the body, and by 8 px past an inline broken image","tags":["inspect","fidelity","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/inspect-render.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:08:33.377651Z","id":"553cea094f6a009f90bf7ad326e6f9ec970b48bbb63b18e682d87189156d7c95","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"647958f22844 commits web/e2e/inspect.spec.ts, which runs renderViewport in Chromium through ?app=1&inspect=1 on a hidden draft from POST /api/drafts, subdomain and sandbox frames, with and without requestAnimationFrame: the PNG is the viewport's size and, scrolled to 200 px above a blue block, shows green in its first 196 rows and only blue from row 204; maxBytes 60% re-renders at 195x400; maxBytes 50 answers 'the screenshot is over 50 bytes even at 0.125 scale'. npx playwright test e2e/inspect.spec.ts --repeat-each 2: 16 passed. The margin-collapse and broken-image offsets it found are concern 5099ca0b.","supersedes":"d82ce354e2cbe7b1c54e512a57351ba028214d51ebc5775af4150f2aea93a0a1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/inspect-render.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:21:00.563340Z","id":"869a0a4398daabb2284225fa5cc1b70045e435e5da19f35d81dcae7ae238eeb9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"renderViewport now renders the document element as a flow-root, and a broken image's glyph keeps the image's exact box with vertical-align text-bottom when it has alt text. Chromium, built clip part, marker position page vs PNG: collapsed first-child margin 40/40 (was 72), body position:relative 56/56 (was 72), default body margin with h1 80/80 (was 102), scrolled 142/142 (was 166), broken inline image with alt 21/21 (was 24), with CSS size 18/18 (was 22), without alt 46/46, display:block 40/40. npx playwright test e2e/inspect.spec.ts: 10 passed, including 'subdomain|sandbox: the PNG places content where the page does, past a collapsed first-child margin and a broken inline image'.","supersedes":"5099ca0b15b3dac207c88b31247e6ad33fdf96de9d8039b273ae5528f1f32965","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:20:06.897924Z","id":"5915312b570e50aa1956de52563df5c533fd6d8ea7278cc287fdb86442ee6af5","body":{"detail":"node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs after npm run build at f1c07f346b12 with other agents' uncommitted work in the tree: artifact 65479/64832, host 6937/6464, bridge 5933/5824, partCaps 8952/8773. The clax:test case, the test part's entry in __CLAX_PARTS__ (web/bridge/src/parts-url.ts) and claxHost.runTests with testsMessage (web/shell/src/app/host.ts) account for part of the bridge and host growth; the rest is other changes. The new test part itself (2418 gzip bytes) is loaded only by the inspect view and has no budget key in web/perf/bundle-budget.json.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":347},"end":{"line":350},"content_hash":"e836bdcd6dfd7b32039ad199de2c748790ee7c379f5d4041d906ee2ec538f435"},"summary":"With the test part's wiring the bundle gate is over budget: eager bridge 5933 gzip bytes (budget 5824), app host 6937 (6464)","tags":["web","bundle","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:23:43.842840Z","id":"f0971320cf896e16f03b1f5ef8bf42afca3daf95c93ff8545f31471719bb1315","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"5915312b570e50aa1956de52563df5c533fd6d8ea7278cc287fdb86442ee6af5","summary":"Measured at 647958f22844 after scripts/build-web.sh, node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs: eager bridge 5933 (budget 5824), app host 6937 (6464), also artifact 65479 (64832) and caps part 8952 (8773) from the net/sample/device commits. By the rule of 647958f22844 (measured + at least 32, rounded up to 64): bridge 6016, host 7040, artifact 65536, partCaps 9024.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/capabilities.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:28:47.146912Z","id":"6be1e7ecd5f8191dfdd6b1384fcdc8f22f9c60b452405b081d7b2cc73f72ec52","body":{"detail":"web/contract/0.2.61/files.d.ts declares files.read/list/download over a Claude Code project; Clax's device capability (clax-extensions.d.ts `Device.Files`) declares pick/save under the same name. A page written for claude.ai that declares {\"files\": {\"project\": …}} gets Clax's namespace in the Clax app (capability_removed on read) instead of null. The name is fixed by the real-applications spec, section C5 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-real-apps-design.md).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":16},"end":{"line":21},"content_hash":"ed5e2bf223f8951806c5d5f2d282004a2a06423b9ef546998a9e5bdfe39da150"},"suggested_fix":"Serve the device namespace only when the declaration has no `project` key, or rename it (for example `deviceFiles`) in the spec and the agent's prompt.","summary":"Clax's `files` device capability takes the name of claude.ai's `files` (project files), with different members","tags":["v1","contract","device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/capabilities.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:32:07.709255Z","id":"d7cdba8889ad2e22ffa2e6ac07bc7f108714c4ce19d6812578e4833851e17520","body":{"detail":"Today the collision bites only in the Clax app: a claude.ai page that declares files gets {pick, save} instead of null, so its feature check passes and files.read throws. Outside the app use('files') still resolves null (served.device is false). The name appears in web/bridge/src/capabilities.ts:18, web/shell/src/caps/{registry,availability,device,device-link}.ts, web/contract/clax-extensions.d.ts, docs/contract.md, device_host.dart and device_grants.dart words, and their tests; renaming to `file` (or `picker`) now costs one commit, later it breaks every app made with it.","kind":"comment","references":"6be1e7ecd5f8191dfdd6b1384fcdc8f22f9c60b452405b081d7b2cc73f72ec52","summary":"Renaming is cheap now: about ten references, no app uses it yet","tags":["v1-review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/capabilities.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:39:13.330035Z","id":"93fe090be1c0dd7db7108d1553e46fb230be27cdaf391356ad49216d6776826d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Renamed the device capability to `file` in the shell, bridge, d.ts, contract, prompt copies and Dart; `files` resolves null again. bridge/test/use.test.ts passes (vitest 660 passed).","supersedes":"6be1e7ecd5f8191dfdd6b1384fcdc8f22f9c60b452405b081d7b2cc73f72ec52","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:29:43.657161Z","id":"e2ec3a3253647a39e69bd2d9c6afc87211445abd87f271ace27bfd94f22af9ab","body":{"detail":"The owner saw a solid area rectangle stuck over the macOS app after a drag. In Playwright's WebKit and Chromium a drag that starts in the content frame and is released anywhere, even outside the viewport, still delivers mouseup to the frame and picks (web/e2e/drag-release.spec.ts), so that case did not reproduce there. onOut and onBlur drop a drag whose release was lost once the page sees the pointer leave with the button up or loses focus, but a release the WKWebView never forwards, with the pointer staying off the page and the window keeping focus, still leaves the rectangle drawn until the next move over the page. To check: in the macOS app, draw an area and release over the comment bar, then outside the window. If it sticks, the app would have to report a mouse's release too (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart _attest returns early for PointerDeviceKind.mouse) and the shell forward it to the bridge to end the drag.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":742},"end":{"line":765},"content_hash":"3dba8f2acb407cae75274966a0b2afac1cd949ee2b3f61398ea21593c08cc4fc"},"summary":"Unverified in the macOS app: whether a mouse drag released over the comment bar or outside the window reaches the page as a mouseup","tags":["comment-mode","macos","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/harness.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:55:21.692427Z","id":"7658e09c176669f2a088bcf4e33335fecd20f9bbc79c2dbb542d7ece1f56e1fe","body":{"detail":"runMigration (web/bridge/src/harness.ts:300-325) is ordered by claxHost.runMigration once the inspect view's page has greeted (ready); by then index.html's scripts have run and may still be running. A page that writes db documents on load (seeding defaults, saving a counter, normalising a shape) does so in the old or new code's shape, concurrently with migrate.js, both on the draft's copy and in the live run of spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md §8.2 step 7. A migration that reads, transforms and sets a document can lose or overwrite the page's write. Options: load a page that does not run the app (an empty document of the draft) for the migration, or document that pages must not write on load.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":300},"end":{"line":325},"content_hash":"037607d87835d7c7a46dc41e73e31400da1317fd3883c36587ef66e20c9bd741"},"summary":"migrate.js runs after the page's own scripts, in the same document, so a page that writes documents as it loads races the migration","tags":["bundles","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/harness.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:58:52.040395Z","id":"589a0a2e442bc5b9da0d1b9b38277e5a0d6ed84faa525608c377f91252830534","body":{"detail":"message(e) (harness.ts:53) calls String(e) for a non-Error. For `throw {toString() { throw this }}` (or a Proxy that throws on conversion), runMigration's catch rethrows from message(e), answerMigration's catch calls message(e) on the same value and throws again, and nothing is posted; WebViewInspector waits total + answerLimit and returns InspectorError 'it did not answer'. The run still ends, but with a misleading reason and 10 s late. A message() that wraps String(e) in try/catch (falling back to 'a value that is not an Error') closes it.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":332},"end":{"line":344},"content_hash":"3ff78f914227ccef489f1799754a7a3472a9d2768271ba6f12cec330d096776d"},"summary":"A thrown value whose String() throws leaves clax:migrate unanswered; the app then sees a timeout instead of the migration's failure","tags":["bundles","review:BW","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/harness.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:09:18.011235Z","id":"a86af24759ef3004753434f7c9189baf0452aaccbe0582a94010825082c9ff47","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: clax:migrate is honoured only in the clax-migrate frame, where the bridge writes <plaintext hidden> before the page's markup parses, so no page script runs beside migrate.js. Evidence: npx playwright test e2e/inspect-tests.spec.ts, 12 passed, including 'runMigration imports migrate.js and runs it on the page's db, in a page whose own markup never runs' (boot/seen null, no buttons, empty title) in both frame modes; web/bridge/test/bridge-migrate.test.ts passes.","supersedes":"7658e09c176669f2a088bcf4e33335fecd20f9bbc79c2dbb542d7ece1f56e1fe","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/harness.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:09:18.012603Z","id":"18cdd0b3e96d592c300130863ca5631274240e3982df790e2c26fdbd49c3c018","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: message() catches a conversion that throws and says 'a value that cannot be shown'. Evidence: web/bridge/test/harness.test.ts 'reports a thrown error, a file that does not load, no default export and a db that fails' (a thrown object whose toString throws answers 'the migration failed: a value that cannot be shown'); npx vitest run: 1689 passed.","supersedes":"589a0a2e442bc5b9da0d1b9b38277e5a0d6ed84faa525608c377f91252830534","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/anchor.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:39:50.184034Z","id":"45a0f9462fa2ca55e1efeff79e7fef881410cc558e76688719fbbd3e06c7af7f","body":{"detail":"textIndex concatenates the data of adjacent text nodes, and buildElementAnchor (line 142) cuts the anchor's quote straight from that text. Block or inline siblings with no whitespace node between them read run together wherever the quote is shown: the app composer's quote line and the Flutter peek label (web/shell/src/app/label.ts anchorLabel, from anchor.quote), and thread cards. Reproduced in Chromium with a row <div><b>Mon</b><span>5 km</span></div>: the state message's draft.label is “Mon5 km”. Present since e89877ff; the stored quote must stay equal to idx.text for findQuote, so the separator cannot simply be added to the index.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":30},"end":{"line":48},"content_hash":"173c494591ba8c15c966d6f2661108f1cfc888fc2d2cfdc28b35c7c9f8661011"},"suggested_fix":"Keep anchor.quote as is for re-anchoring and give the label its own words: have the bridge send a display text for the pick (text nodes joined by spaces and collapsed, as textPrefix at line 196 already does) in PickDesc, and have anchorLabel and composerQuote prefer it.","summary":"An element's quote joins its text nodes with nothing between them, so <b>Mon</b><span>5 km</span> is quoted and labelled “Mon5 km”","tags":["ux","comments","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/anchor.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:48:29.513945Z","id":"822d9bfd67bc57d5639c9644ca2da7e18839d053d0a582ba0f9c5d4a4ec63b62","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Picks now carry PickDesc.text, the element's text spaced between elements; the app's draft label, the shell composer's quote and the app's thread labels use it, and the quote and text index are unchanged. Evidence: web/bridge/test/describe.test.ts (<b>Mon</b><span>5 km</span> -> 'Mon 5 km'), web/shell/src/app/host.test.ts 'shows a pick's spaced text…', web/e2e/app-mode.spec.ts 'a picked row of elements is labelled…' pass; npx vitest run: 1816 passed; playwright app-mode, hold-drag, comment-targets, comments, comment-flows: 83 passed. Labels after a reload are a separate concern on web/shell/src/app/host.ts:414:417.","supersedes":"45a0f9462fa2ca55e1efeff79e7fef881410cc558e76688719fbbd3e06c7af7f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/routes.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T05:19:28.066701Z","id":"2f8ad8cd45684b223ce3c86e528273df32681d624af306ebdf5eab2528a84361","body":{"detail":"node scripts/bundle-size.mjs after npm run build at 647958f22844: artifact 65757 (budget 65728; 65753 at 647958f22844 already, from the composer's dropped-post notice), app host 8927 (8826; 8806 before), eager bridge 6150 (6144; 6106 before), caps part 9875 (9664; 9588 before). The route watch (routes.ts) is ~290 gzip bytes of the caps part, loaded only on the app shell's welcome; the eager bridge carries only the clax:back type and its case.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":53},"end":{"line":60},"content_hash":"b070c74cbd726c8b19f5d198006b0bcf63a5207d51919fd2eb76181a8547f032"},"suggested_fix":"Raise the four budgets by the measured growth, or trim routes.ts and the host's trail code before raising.","summary":"The page's pushState routes and the composer's dropped-post notice (647958f22844) put four bundles over web/perf/bundle-budget.json","tags":["perf","bundle-budget","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/routes.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T05:19:28.066745Z","id":"547198edee7bfd64abe7dca8c8b1e4bd209bc3a44f7b4d2041bfc78a868ca7e5","body":{"detail":"back() replaces the frame's current entry with the lower route's URL and state (in place, as the shell's fragment back does with location.replace), so the joint session history keeps the real entry of that route below it: from routes [load, r1, r2], the app's back leaves [load, r1, r1]. The page's own back then traverses to r1 again (no popstate change it can see), and only its second press reaches load. The app's own back is unaffected.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":53},"end":{"line":60},"content_hash":"b070c74cbd726c8b19f5d198006b0bcf63a5207d51919fd2eb76181a8547f032"},"suggested_fix":"Return with history.go(to - depth) when no fragment entry was made since the push (the bridge would have to count fragment entries too), or accept it as the shell's fragment back does.","summary":"After the app's back to a route, the page's own history.back() lands on an entry of the same route, so one press of the page's back does nothing","tags":["navigation","deferred","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/routes.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T05:31:59.457304Z","id":"35cad125ee523804967a65134a292be114184f8347e11cb36d5267ecfb654690","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: the shell's back to a route traverses the page's own entries (history.go) while they are its routes' alone, so the page's next own back reaches the route below. Evidence: npx vitest run bridge/test/routes.test.ts: 3 passed, including 'reports the page's pushes and its own back, and takes the page back through its own entries on the shell's back' (failed before the fix); npx playwright test e2e/app-mode.spec.ts --project rest: 18 passed, its pushState test now pressing the page's own back after the app's (fails at app-mode.spec.ts:375 with the routes.ts of 647958f22844; 5 repeats passed with the fix). After a fragment entry among the routes the move stays in place.","supersedes":"547198edee7bfd64abe7dca8c8b1e4bd209bc3a44f7b4d2041bfc78a868ca7e5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/routes.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T05:31:59.463464Z","id":"0c013a35b0092b53b7d1fd1313025c578286b1e6033c6c4aa430821c2816aade","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Under budget: artifact and eager bridge trimmed back under, app host and caps part raised by the measured growth. Evidence: node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs after npm run build at 647958f22844 exits 0: artifact 65719 (budget 65728), eager bridge 6135 (6144), app host 9003 (9088), caps 9957 (10048).","supersedes":"2f8ad8cd45684b223ce3c86e528273df32681d624af306ebdf5eab2528a84361","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:09:51.176837Z","id":"0e9f60d93ec452b0af57f2dfea40a11b3f679f24b545c680704104f563ee1286","body":{"detail":"While a page's own scripts hold up the parse, comment mode and use() wait for it with no sign to the viewer. This needs a protocol addition: the bridge reports that it is waiting.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":40},"end":{"line":43},"content_hash":"21752b7263ca6b42a47eaef764ade6ba85f1d6e668c14f22c1a65849231a7eb0"},"suggested_fix":"Have the bridge report a wait for the parse, and the shell show a hint ('waiting for the page').","summary":"The shell shows nothing while the bridge waits for the page's parse","supersedes":"aa1344c28799fc184a41e2f18b50fc3751794d662961edb93a0ce5c4df9f3d0b","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/chrome.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:42:15.037153Z","id":"0aa3232c97b5cc4b101848e1ebbcceea507c151d81144bba165301a42836845f","body":{"detail":"reportChrome resamples on a MutationObserver (childList, class and style attributes), scroll and resize, so a background that changes through a CSS animation or transition, a :hover or media-query state, or an image or font load that moves which element sits at an edge, is not reported until the next of those events. backdrop() reads only background-color: a background-image (a gradient header, a photo) is skipped and the walk takes the parent's colour, and a computed colour in another space (oklch(), lab(), color(display-p3 …)) is treated as not opaque. Checked in Chromium by web/e2e/app-mode.spec.ts 'the page's edge colours reach the app as chrome' (a color-mix(in srgb) header computes to color(srgb …) and is read as #808080).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":44},"end":{"line":58},"content_hash":"a3c075f28a649678eb9778df797f16e06ca531213eaa7f444b71614e6b11ba0b"},"suggested_fix":"If pages show wrong bands, add a ResizeObserver on the edge elements and transitionend/animationend listeners, and sample a background-image's dominant colour only if it proves common.","summary":"The edge sampler misses changes with no DOM mutation, scroll or resize, and reads only rgb()/rgba()/color(srgb) background colours","tags":["app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T10:16:28.945493Z","id":"4dc64d66b9ee8bb2df90e65b02846415cb5892baaa1de7204bd4826b6ba578cf","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: the bridge posts clax:wait around a need that waits for the parse, the app host posts pageWait after 400 ms, and the comment bar says 'Waiting for the page…'; bridge-parse-gate.test.ts, host.test.ts and app_screen_test 'a slow page…' pass (bazelisk test //web:unit //apps/clax_app:ui_app_screen_test)","supersedes":"0e9f60d93ec452b0af57f2dfea40a11b3f679f24b545c680704104f563ee1286","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T10:16:29.037474Z","id":"0ce444da3d34aec0e161c409c8a4f68a72550d7af76ae96d22c07d222a8e74a3","body":{"detail":"//web:bundle_size after 647958f22844: eager bridge 6268, budget 6272. The next eager-bridge change needs a saving elsewhere in bridge.ts or a budget raise.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":146},"end":{"line":155},"content_hash":"eddfd1edecc52349368f252eb2843306b9da1a0901ba29b6641dd88b0decdefd"},"summary":"The eager bridge is 4 gzip bytes under its budget after clax:wait (6268 of 6272 in web/perf/bundle-budget.json)","tags":["bundle-size","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:36:01.867588Z","id":"f11d0986599a5e37312294c604f2b58048da4a6ab09d5f5c4357f69a1243af03","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e2ec3a3253647a39e69bd2d9c6afc87211445abd87f271ace27bfd94f22af9ab","summary":"Still open after f1c07f346b12: the app does not report a mouse release the WKWebView missed. Flutter sees no mouse events over the WebView (a platform view), so the report has to come from AppKit (WindowBridge's leftMouseDown monitor in apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/WindowBridge.swift, plus a leftMouseUp one), and attestPointer 'up' (web/shell/src/app/host.ts) ends no drag: the shell would need a new call the bridge answers with endDrag. Such a release, sent through Dart and runJavaScript, can reach the page before WebKit's own queued mouseup and drop an area pick the page was about to take, so it should wait until the real drag is seen to stick (the apps/clax_app macOS chrome test's real drag).","tags":["macos","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:50:19.976995Z","id":"9b7b8805db18be70b09e39f22df70a70c1548e387267c1d58c5dd61628b472cc","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e2ec3a3253647a39e69bd2d9c6afc87211445abd87f271ace27bfd94f22af9ab","summary":"apps/clax_app/integration_test/mac_chrome_test.dart now draws an area in the page and lets go over the sidebar, and expects the area pick when the events go through AppKit's queue (an active app). bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_mac_chrome --test_env=CLAX_MAC_SHOTS_DIR=$PWD/target/flutter-app/mac at f1c07f346b12 PASSED, on a locked display (the app inactive: windows drawn from their layers, events handed to their views, key checks skipped; see docs/usage.md): events went to the views directly and no area was picked, so this run says nothing either way; it needs the owner's run on an unlocked Mac.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/chrome.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:50:19.978735Z","id":"3a645aa875798048d033fb5890fe83e19d108680e941fdb00c7f95f2c4623722","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"0aa3232c97b5cc4b101848e1ebbcceea507c151d81144bba165301a42836845f","summary":"The light/dark media-query case is fixed by 647958f22844 (the bridge samples again on prefers-color-scheme's change; web/bridge/test/chrome.test.ts 'samples again when the light or dark appearance changes'); apps/clax_app's chrome test had shown the app's band in the dark page's colour over the same page turned light. Animations, :hover, loads and other colour spaces stand.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/bridge.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T06:03:52.083795Z","id":"81e89616fb306aed49102b31a367cc900de0bd496d9eeeed9176360b9125fbd1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"The part loader tables are built from the part list (parts-url.ts loadParts, bridge.ts onNeed wrappers): eager bridge 6268 -> 6172 gzip bytes of its 6272 budget, unchanged. bazelisk test //web:bundle_size at 647958f22844 passed: gallery 27960 of 28096, artifact 64777 of 66048 (1271 left, 1.9%), app host 8379 of 9088, eager bridge 6172 of 6272 (100 left, 1.6%), transport 2015 of 2038, parts comment 14643 of 14720, clip 17351 of 17408, caps 11343 of 11392; web/perf/bundle-budget.json unchanged.","supersedes":"0ce444da3d34aec0e161c409c8a4f68a72550d7af76ae96d22c07d222a8e74a3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/parts-url.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:20:14.519054Z","id":"4e9f5b3c4cd605c428971868d9d09176a51301d140e5e046eca760b0095a4e53","body":{"detail":"Since 647958f22844 loadParts makes a loader only for the names __CLAX_PARTS__ holds, and the bridge's table (bridge/src/bridge.ts:157) maps over those, so a missing part is undefined and parts.<name>() throws a TypeError in the caller. For the test part that is the clax:test and clax:migrate handlers (bridge.ts:409, 415): they no longer post 'the test harness did not load', and the app waits out its limit. Before, every part had a loader that rejected 'no URL for the <name> part'. The build's guard (web/vite.bridge.config.ts:10) checks six names and not test, although scripts/build-parts.mjs:21 builds seven. parts-url.ts itself has no unit test: vitest aliases clax-bridge-parts to parts-static.ts (web/vitest.config.ts:12).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":18},"end":{"line":27},"content_hash":"3aadf41d0999cd74c4e337f1302c5652e2c68641ddf6b36e5f6cd313fbb154b9"},"suggested_fix":"Add test to the guard in vite.bridge.config.ts (or check every key of Parts there), so a build without a part fails at build time.","summary":"A part the build leaves out of __CLAX_PARTS__ now has no loader at all, so its first need throws instead of being answered","tags":["review","bridge","minor","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/parts-url.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:14:24.201294Z","id":"00d5db18e30bf30847115093df64d113108cfd25a8e2de8e3e6982ac7f5684ee","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed in 647958f22844 (its message names other work as well; the change is web/bridge/src/parts-url.ts, the part names, web/vite.bridge.config.ts and web/bridge/test/parts-url.test.ts) and 647958f22844 (the names moved to web/bridge/src/part-names.ts, outside parts/, as bridge/test/split.test.ts requires): loadParts makes a loader for every name in PART_NAMES, which the types tie to Parts, and a part the build named no file for rejects 'no URL for the <name> part'; the bridge build's guard checks the same list, test included. bridge/test/parts-url.test.ts (2 passed): every part has a loader when __CLAX_PARTS__ lacks test, which rejects naming it; a load goes beside the bridge script and a retry under ?retry=<n>.","supersedes":"4e9f5b3c4cd605c428971868d9d09176a51301d140e5e046eca760b0095a4e53","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/channel.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:32:18.755649Z","id":"229fd8d5b2a1a567d3c2ec22ecf809f7b19f4ec3485a939c53eeb07912297485","body":{"detail":"With AppState.embed set, the artifact view frames each page at the embed's content origin (web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts decideOrigin, web/shell/src/origin.ts artifactOrigin), e.g. https://<id>.c.clax.invalid or clax://<id>.c. The bridge there reads the shell's origins from its tag's data-origin or else from location.href (web/bridge/src/bridge.ts:190); shellOrigins of a content URL that does not end in .localhost answers that URL's own origin. The content route writes data-origin only for a hosted daemon's content origin (crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs:143-148, the `shell` passed to wrap_page_framed_by), never the embed's shell origin. So acceptFromShell (web/bridge/src/channel.ts:28-33) drops the shell's clax:welcome from https://app.clax.invalid (or clax://app): comment mode, clips and capability calls never start in the app. No user reaches it until the app runs on the core; web/e2e's app transport spec (artifact view loads and a comment posts through the channel) is where it shows first.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":10},"end":{"line":15},"content_hash":"57e86ccda59f36620d166e04c9e38bfc8c3c734989d7dbfcf685612eeb7a6dfd"},"suggested_fix":"In crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs, pass the embed's shell origin as `shell` when AppState.embed is set (s.embed.as_ref().map(|e| e.shell.clone()), after the hosted case), so the bridge tag names it in data-origin.","summary":"In the Clax app a page's bridge takes orders from no shell: shellOrigins names the page's own content origin, and the core writes no data-origin for the embed's shell","tags":["app","origins","bridge","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/channel.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:52:53.542434Z","id":"8a9a5aa3fa7efde34259dbd85959bb205694f5f9dfb9e32d8b7583684a55e6d6","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs:144-148 sets `shell` only from s.hosted with a content origin, and it is the only caller of clax_core::wrap::wrap_page_framed_by with a shell; drafts are never wrapped (crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs:446). crates/clax-embed/tests/embed.rs an_owner_call_creates_and_a_content_frame_reads_its_page reads the page with As::Content and checks only its frame-ancestors, so nothing asserts the bridge tag. With data-origin=\"clax://app\", web/bridge/src/channel.ts shellOrigins answers [\"clax://app\"] (URL host of a non-special scheme), which is the e.origin the Mac spike (apps/clax_app/integration_test/scheme_spike.dart:394, parent.postMessage(r, cfg.shell)) shows WebKit delivering. The wrap cache (WrapCache, keyed by artifact, version and file) needs no new key: the shell origin is fixed for the life of an AppState.","kind":"comment","references":"229fd8d5b2a1a567d3c2ec22ecf809f7b19f4ec3485a939c53eeb07912297485","suggested_fix":"In content.rs lookup(): `let shell = s.hosted.as_ref().filter(|h| h.content_origin().is_some()).map(|h| h.origin.clone()).or_else(|| s.embed.as_ref().map(|e| e.shell.clone()));` and its comment: 'Content framed by a shell on another origin names it: a hosted daemon's public origin, or the app's shell origin (AppState.embed).' Update web/bridge/src/bridge.ts:10-12 and :188-189 to name the app's shell origin too. Test in crates/clax-embed/tests/embed.rs: `a_page_served_to_a_content_frame_names_the_apps_shell_for_its_bridge`: open, publish \"<title>t</title>hi\", then for \"/v/1/\" and \"/v/1/index.html\" a head(\"GET\", path, As::Content) with host Some(id) answers 200 and its body contains `data-origin=\"clax://app\"></script>` exactly once; in crates/clax-server/tests/shell_boot.rs an_embedded_core_marks_every_shell_document_and_frames_content_on_its_origin, also read `/v/1/` with Host `{id}.localhost:{port}` from `embedded` (contains data-origin=\"clax://app\") and `/v/1/` of the plain daemon's `pid` (contains no data-origin), so the browser path stays as it is.","summary":"Confirmed against the code: the fix is one fallback in crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs lookup(), and its test is a content frame of the embedded core","tags":["review","app","bridge","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/channel.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:44:55.893651Z","id":"47dc3cb24e9071096ab8654991ab68cf3599638f071d9ae9c14524f92e91f891","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f2284459b2440c3504082626f77bdacfae","summary":"Fixed: crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs lookup() falls back to AppState.embed's shell origin, so the bridge tag carries data-origin=\"clax://app\". bazelisk test //crates/clax-embed:embed passed with a_page_served_to_a_content_frame_names_the_apps_shell_for_its_bridge (/v/1/ and /v/1/about.html, the tag exactly once; /v/1/index.html answers 308 to /v/1/), and //crates/clax-server:integration__3 with shell_boot an_embedded_core_marks_every_shell_document_and_frames_content_on_its_origin (embedded content names clax://app, the plain daemon's names no data-origin); both failed before the fix.","supersedes":"229fd8d5b2a1a567d3c2ec22ecf809f7b19f4ec3485a939c53eeb07912297485","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:44.761161Z","id":"af2a67c68dfd44e0e94b44cca50c4b76728a9c77e371e0997ba8e8da12760e4d","body":{"detail":"CommentMode.set writes `documentElement.style.cursor = on ? \"crosshair\" : \"\"`, so a page (or, through the Chrome extension's overlay, which reuses CommentMode in web/extension/src/content/overlay-app.ts, any web site) that set an inline `cursor` on <html> loses it after one round of comment mode. The class otherwise takes care never to change the page (the overlay lives in a shadow root, lines 17-20).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":109},"end":{"line":109},"content_hash":"99d8b2365cc37f5236bdd30e5c68b661910e490899018111e766b4b5bd4bb1f4"},"suggested_fix":"Save `documentElement.style.cursor` (and its priority) when the mode turns on and restore it when it turns off, or draw the crosshair from the overlay's shadow root CSS instead of the page's own style attribute.","summary":"Turning comment mode off wipes any inline cursor the page itself set on <html>","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:16.140046Z","id":"0c155b229b2e1c01791b56bf95e373b1c617f06abbef8241e8506e14ef24ebcc","body":{"detail":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts:109 `this.doc.documentElement.style.cursor = on ? \"crosshair\" : \"\";` with no saved prior value; web/extension/src/content/overlay-app.ts:13 imports CommentMode and line 229 instantiates it on arbitrary sites. Kind suggestion fits.","kind":"comment","references":"af2a67c68dfd44e0e94b44cca50c4b76728a9c77e371e0997ba8e8da12760e4d","summary":"confirmed: set(false) writes documentElement.style.cursor = \"\", erasing any inline cursor the page set","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:24:50.684371Z","id":"27e8eafe89df3b7a047401a9738deb348a9edd078e90ebb253c53c58cb15f0e6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:8bb0abadd","summary":"Fixed: CommentMode saves and restores the page's inline <html> cursor and priority; web/bridge/test/comment-mode.test.ts passes; //web:e2e_chrome_overlay passes.","supersedes":"af2a67c68dfd44e0e94b44cca50c4b76728a9c77e371e0997ba8e8da12760e4d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
